00:02:05,963 --> 00:02:08,656
that the case? Because these models, when

51
00:02:09,008 --> 00:02:10,643
they receive some input,

52
00:02:11,188 --> 00:02:14,282
need to perform many calculations in

53
00:02:14,394 --> 00:02:17,200
parallel in order to produce that output.

54
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:20,470
And it turns out that GPUs are amazing at

55
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:23,179
performing many calculations in parallel.

56
00:02:24,254 --> 00:02:27,479
A CPU, on the other hand, can switch between

57
00:02:27,479 --> 00:02:30,191
different tasks but can only process them in

58
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:33,738
sequence in the end. That's why GPUs are

59
00:02:33,802 --> 00:02:36,337
preferred to handle all these computations

60
00:02:36,434 --> 00:02:39,130
that need to be performed in parallel when

61
00:02:39,258 --> 00:02:40,510
performing inference.

62
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,960
So in an ideal world, we have a great GPU,

63
00:02:44,473 --> 00:02:46,255
but a CPU will also do.

