00:03:04,933 --> 00:03:06,891
typically also have VRAM, and that's

71
00:03:07,003 --> 00:03:09,811
preferably because the GPU has more direct

72
00:03:09,827 --> 00:03:13,036
and quicker access to the VRAM than to the

73
00:03:13,181 --> 00:03:16,005
regular system memory. But again, if you

74
00:03:16,005 --> 00:03:19,070
don't have a GPU, regular RAM, your regular

75
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,124
system memory will also do.

76
00:03:21,862 --> 00:03:23,705
Why do we need that? Well, because the

77
00:03:23,721 --> 00:03:26,959
model, all its parameters essentially, and

78
00:03:27,055 --> 00:03:29,844
also the context window, which essentially

79
00:03:29,956 --> 00:03:32,809
is the chat history, your input messages and

80
00:03:32,906 --> 00:03:33,739
the output messages,

81
00:03:34,348 --> 00:03:37,297
all that must be loaded into memory during

82
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:40,984
